  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1220 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nBy Wednesday, the remnants of PCT 5 are forecast to be moving over \neast-central Texas. Some of that moisture is forecast to affect part \nof South Central Texas especially areas along and east of Highway \n77. As mentioned above, rainfall accumulations are likely to \nconcentrate to the east of the I-35 corridor and likely to areas \nalong and east of Highway 77. High temperatures are forecast to be \nvery similar for the long term period at least from Wednesday \nthrough the weekend. There are new opportunities for rain on \nThursday through Saturday as an upper level disturbance moves across \nthe northern Gulf. Rain chances favoring the Coastal Plains along \nwith seabreeze activity.",
